    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math learning by adapting to individual needs—like explaining concepts in simple terms or generating practice problems tailored to a student’s level. They could also create interactive simulations for visual learners, such as showing how calculus works with real-world examples like sports or art. This makes math less intimidating and more relatable."
